    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0157",
      "sequence": 169,
      "meaning": "Hearing horse and rider rushing near, the boar flees with the speed of wind. The king immediately aims an arrow, but as he watches, the beast merges with the earth; repeatedly targeted, it saves itself by trickery, appearing and disappearing as the angry king follows. It draws him deep into an impenetrable wilderness where neither elephant nor horse can manage. Though alone and sorely afflicted, the king refuses to abandon its trail. The boar finally enters a deep mountain cave; finding it inaccessible, the king regrets the chase, turns back, and loses his way in the vast forest. Exhausted, hungry and thirsty, he searches desperately with his horse for river, lake or water until he faints.",
